{"text": "believable", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">bilevable</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">beleevable</i>, equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">believe</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-able</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Capable of being believed; credible.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["IPA", "/b\u026a\u02c8li\u02d0v\u0259bl\u0329/"]]}